## Add collect statistics on feature usages and errors occurs to this app.
Note: Do not change StatisticsCollectorService, just use it.

- How to record feature usage:
    - Definition
```csharp
/// <summary>
/// Records the usage of a feature
/// </summary>
/// <param name="featureName">Name of the feature used</param>
/// <param name="count">Number of times the feature was used</param>
/// <param name="additionalData">Additional data to record</param>
public void RecordFeatureUsage(string featureName, int count = 1, Dictionary<string, object> additionalData = null)
```
    - Example:
```csharp
StatisticsCollectorService.Instance.RecordFeatureUsage("FeatureName");
// With count
StatisticsCollectorService.Instance.RecordFeatureUsage("BulkOperation", 5);
// With additional data
StatisticsCollectorService.Instance.RecordFeatureUsage("ExportFile", 1, new Dictionary<string, object> { 
    { "format", "pdf" }, 
    { "fileSize", 1024 }
});

```
- How to record error:
    - Definition:
```csharp
/// <summary>
/// Records an error that occurred during execution
/// </summary>
/// <param name="errorType">Type of error</param>
/// <param name="errorMessage">Error message</param>
/// <param name="stackTrace">Stack trace of the error</param>
/// <param name="additionalData">Additional data to record</param>
public void RecordError(string errorType, string errorMessage, string stackTrace, Dictionary<string, object> additionalData = null)
```
    - Example
```csharp
try
{
    // Your code
}
catch (Exception ex)
{
    StatisticsCollectorService.Instance.RecordError("OperationFailed", ex.Message, ex.StackTrace);
    throw;
}
```